# Chili Con Carne

Based on Alex’s Aunt’s recipe

{ rating="4" image="chili_con_carne.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2-3 Tbsp [butter]{ ing="butter" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [onion]{ ing="onion" }, chopped and
- [ ] 1/2 [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } (bulb?), chopped
- [ ] 1-2 lbs 80[% lean ground beef]{ ing="lean-ground-beef" }
- [ ] 1.25 cups [canned whole tomatoes]{ ing="canned-whole-tomatoes" }
- [ ] 4 cups [kidney beans]{ ing="kidney-beans" }
- [ ] 1/2 [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp or [more of salt]{ ing="more-of-salt" }
- [ ] 1 can [Hormel chili]{ ing="hormel-chili" } (with or without beans)
- [ ] [Add spices]{ ing="add-spices" } from 2 Alarm Chili Mix (or any boxed chili mix)

## Recipe

1. In a large pot, melt 2-3 tablespoons [butter]{ ing="butter" } then saute the chopped [onion]{ ing="onion" } and [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }
1. Add the ground beed
1. Stir and sauté until [beef]{ ing="lean-ground-beef" } is well done (nice and brown) and all the liquid is evaporated
1. Add the can of [whole tomatoes]{ ing="canned-whole-tomatoes" }, [kidney beans]{ ing="kidney-beans" }, bayleaf, [salt]{ ing="more-of-salt" }, [Hormel chili]{ ing="hormel-chili" }, boxed chili mix
1. Cover and cook for about and hour

## Notes

- *Add the masala ~20 minutes before taking out of the oven to thicken the chili*
- I only added a tiny bit of the red pepper and put the remainder in a dish so people could add it if they wanted it hotter
